You are given a string S containing digits from 0 to 9.

You can select one digit at a time until all digits have been selected.

For every selection, the score obtained is:

selected digit×number of digits remaining after the selection
The total score is the sum of the scores obtained in all selections.

Find the maximum possible total score.

Input Format

The first line contains an integer N, representing the number of digits.

The second line contains a string S of length N, containing digits from 0 to 9.





#include <iostream>
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int n;
    cin>>n;
   string s;
   cin>>s;                       // do not use getline if taking n with string
   sort(s.begin(),s.end());
   int score=0;
   for(int i=n-1;i>=0;i--){
       int current=s[i]-'0';
        n=n-1;
       score+=current*n;
   }
   cout<<score;
    return 0;
}
